                <pb facs="0925" n="837" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg837"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Loomis to Mr.
                            Leishman.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-07-19"><hi rendition="#italic">July 19,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis informs Mr. Leishman that the Department has instructed Mr. Norton to
                    go to Van and Bitlis for the purpose of gathering information regarding the
                    reported massacres of Armenians, and whether American missionaries are in danger
                    there.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
